sections.body:
Even setting aside sampling bias entirely, manual spot-checking has a structural limitation that has nothing to do with how carefully it's done: **it doesn't run again automatically.** A developer who tries five queries today, confirms they look good, and ships a change has validated exactly one snapshot in time. The next change -- a reindex with different parameters, a new embedding model, a chunking strategy tweak, an added metadata filter -- gets no equivalent scrutiny unless someone remembers to manually re-run a similar check, which in practice happens inconsistently at best, especially under any kind of deadline pressure.

```python
def recall_at_k(retrieved, relevant, k):
    top_k = retrieved[:k]
    hits = sum(1 for item in top_k if item in relevant)
    return hits / len(relevant)

golden_dataset = [{"query": f"q{i}", "relevant_ids": {f"d{i}"}} for i in range(1, 6)]

def retrieve_current(query, k):
    responses = {"q1": ["d1"], "q2": ["d2"], "q3": ["x3"], "q4": ["x4"], "q5": ["x5"]}
    return responses[query][:k]

def avg_recall(dataset, retrieve_fn, k):
    scores = [recall_at_k(retrieve_fn(c["query"], k), c["relevant_ids"], k) for c in dataset]
    return sum(scores) / len(scores)

manual_subset = [c for c in golden_dataset if c["query"] in ("q1", "q2")]
print(round(avg_recall(manual_subset, retrieve_current, 1), 3))     # 1.0 -- the two queries a developer happened to try
print(round(avg_recall(golden_dataset, retrieve_current, 1), 3))    # 0.4 -- the real, full picture
```

The developer who happened to manually try q1 and q2 after some index parameter change would see a perfect, reassuring 1.0 and conclude everything is fine -- while the full golden set, covering the same change, reveals a genuine regression affecting the majority of query patterns. This is exactly the same value proposition automated tests provide in software generally, just applied to retrieval quality specifically: an automated check that reruns on every relevant change catches regressions a human's necessarily incomplete, unrepeated manual sampling structurally cannot.

